  "reference": "they would not be such a trouble to me now.\"\nAt last, the prince got tired of the constant reminders of his bad behavior.\nHe wanted to be able to do as he liked, so he threw his ring aside, and thought\nhimself the happiest of men to have got rid of its teasing pricks.\n\"Sir, I'm\nonly a shepherdess and a poor girl,\" she said, \"but I won't marry you,\n\"Do you dislike me?\" asked Prince Darling, annoyed at this answer.\n\"No, my prince,\" replied Celia. \"I notice you are very rich, but what good\nwould richness be to me? If I see you commit wrongdoings every day, I will\ndislike you and even hate you. What will our marriage be like if I am a witness",
